{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/97917-balancing-the-kiths-thoughts","id":97917,"title":"Balancing the kiths: Thoughts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-24T17:50:09-07:00","id":97917,"title":"Balancing the kiths: Thoughts","content":"So, we all know that the kiths, as written, are about as well-balanced as a drunken acrobat on a high line in a hurricane with severe mommy issues. I'm thinking it might be a good idea to work up some houserules to adjust the most egregious examples. <br /> <br /> To that end, what do folks see as the most overpowered/underpowered Kith examples? <br /> <br /> I know that the Shadowsoul blessing is just out of line overpowered. On the other end of the line, I've always felt like Manikins get the short end of the stick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T19:01:04-07:00","id":97977,"title":"","content":"Eh, I've never really felt too fussed about the strengths and weaknesses of many of the Kiths. They're not really a big influence on the game.<br /> <br /> That said, an Elemental Dual Kith Gargantuan is stacking absurd amounts of health.<br /> <br /> Stonebones versus Earthbones has always struck me as a bit funny. Indeed, many of the Elemental Kiths in the core book aren't terribly impressive, but I guess they counter that by having a stellar Blessing.<br /> <br /> On a slightly unreleated note, Beasts have hands down the worst Wyrd Evolutions in Equinox Road. Your reward for hitting high Wyrd is a new Specialty in Animal Ken? Really? Even if you didn't have rather nasty new Curses to cope with, that would be pretty laughable when paired off against things like the Elemental boosts.<br /> <br /> There are a lot, and I mean a lot, of Kiths out there. Most of them seem underpowered, to be honest.<br /> <br /> Is the Shadowsoul Kith the one that gives the option of a free point of Defence even against shooting? Because that always struck me as pretty comparable to Bright One.<br /> <br /> Edit: Heh, that rambled a lot more than I was intending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T19:17:21-07:00","id":97993,"title":"","content":"Shadowsoul is a Fairest kith that gains 9-again on Subterfuge, a bonus equal to their Wyrd to their Intimidate skill, *and* the Contracts of Darkness at Affinity. Compare this to the Manikin, who get a reduction in the untrained penalty for Crafts (which is worthless after spending 3 XP for a dot) and half-affinity on Contracts of Artifice (new dots x5, rather than x6).<br /> <br /> I'm not even going to think about evolutions 'til I can look at the list of the kiths without shuddering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T21:10:57-07:00","id":98057,"title":"","content":"I have two Kiths I changed in my Houserule Document. I am gonna copy it with my note on Elementals so it makes sense:<br /> <br /> <b>Elementals</b>:<br /> <br /> <b>Curse</b>: The Elemental Curse does not apply to those Attributes or Skills when used with with Elemental Affinity contracts, but do apply to non Affinity Contracts and Court Contracts as usual.<br /> <br /> Reason: The Elemental Curse is harsh, and it makes sense it would apply less when addressing natural elements.<br /> <br /> <b>Manikin</b> <b>Kith</b>: Manikins also get Contracts of Animation at x5 as well as Artifice, and Animation and Artifice Count as Elemental Affinity Contracts for purposes of the weakness above.<br /> <br /> Reason: See above, plus the Manikin Kith could probably use a second contract anyway in case Artifice is not desired, since a Manikin with Craft 1 and no Artifice effectively has no power.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fairest</b><br /> <br /> <b>Shadowsoul Kith</b>: Shadowsouls do not get Darkness as an Affinity Contract.<br /> <br /> Reason: Have you read it their blessing? Jesus. Also, Contracts of Darkness have very little to with Shadowsouls MO. It feels tacked on.<br /> <br /> <b>Autumn Court</b>:<br /> <br /> <b>Mantle</b>: The Mantle 1 ability for Autumn Court not only applies to any Contract using Occult, but also Low Magic (from <b>Second Sight</b>) or Rites of Things that Must Not Be (also <b>Second Sight</b>) or any other supernatural effect the Autumn Courtier is using Occult in the roll for, such as Exorcism.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I examined Minstrel Kith as overpowered, but given the limitations I decided to not nerf it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T23:13:12-07:00","id":98131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/97917-balancing-the-kiths-thoughts?p=98057#post98057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have two Kiths I changed in my Houserule Document. I am gonna copy it with my note on Elementals so it makes sense:<br /> <br /> <b>Elementals</b>:<br /> <br /> <b>Curse</b>: The Elemental Curse does not apply to those Attributes or Skills when used with with Elemental Affinity contracts, but do apply to non Affinity Contracts and Court Contracts as usual.<br /> <br /> Reason: The Elemental Curse is harsh, and it makes sense it would apply less when addressing natural elements.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was actually errata'd in the core book where it does exactly that - officially the curse does not apply to affinity contracts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T01:59:51-07:00","id":98204,"title":"","content":"Oh. I thought I half remembered that as a rule but could not find it in any books. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T17:43:56-07:00","id":100492,"title":"","content":"I'd probably do something similar to that, Baron. For Shadowsouls, one move I'd make is to rule that their kith bonus to Intimidate only counts toward mundane uses. I've seen too much cheese where a mid-Wyrd player used Contracts with Intimidate at a base at a level where nobody could even *try* to break free.<br /> <br /> I like that Manikin fix, too. Gives them a bonus even after they've bought the Contract(s). Maybe tweak part of it with 9-again on some crafts rolls and/or a free Crafts specialty indicating the method of their manufacture.<br /> <br /> Any other kiths that folks think are over- or underpowered? I need input!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","user":"HobbitGuy1420","date":". 03-27-2014, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T21:33:25-07:00","id":100602,"title":"","content":"I participated in a fairly long thread about this on RPG.net. I'm not sure I care to repeat the whole thing. Though if you're having trouble finding it I can get a link for it.<br /> <br /> In general though, I think a lot of the physical based Kiths have incredibly weak bonuses; esp. the Beasts. A lot of the Wizened Kiths seem to be off. Some are incredibly good, others are pathetically weak, and many are extremely niche powers that don't do anything for a large number of concepts that could fall into those Kiths (Brewers and Soldiers as great examples).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T00:36:05-07:00","id":100636,"title":"","content":"The Wizened Kith Oracle ( <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Panomancy) </span></span>is probably the most pathetic of all: common sense merit. Any ideas to modify it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T01:03:29-07:00","id":100640,"title":"","content":"I disagree highly with that assessment. It isn't the Common Sense Merit, it just works on the same mechanics. Most importantly unlike the Common Sense Merit, the player gets to pick when to use it, rather than it getting used when the ST decides. And it is at least something that fits any Oracle based concept. It's also easy enough to use the GMC version of Common Sense instead since it has better guidelines for player motivated usage.<br /> <br /> If you want to look at the most pathetic of all? Look at the Soldier: a free Weaponry Specialty in blades.<br /> <br /> That's it. Soldier that uses guns, or a bow, or a mace? Nothing. This is something that literally any character could already have with their base creation points if they want it.<br /> <br /> Compare that to the Draconic (not that I like them much either) who get +1 to all Brawl rolls, and can spend 1 Glamour, once a scene, to re-roll a Brawl roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T02:28:11-07:00","id":100652,"title":"","content":"Fair enough.<br /> Also, the Wizened Drudge Kith doesn\u00b4t need to expend glamour to activate <i>Unseen Labor </i>when they are using it to furfill the Reaper\u00b4s pledge. I think it makes sense, considering otherwise they wouldn\u00b4t get any benefit from mending hundred if shoes in one night for a simple dish of food with 1 point of glamour.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T17:35:25-07:00","id":104468,"title":"","content":"I'd actually disagree about the soldier kith specialty. At least the way I would run things, a specialty in bladed weapons is too broad to have from character creation and I'd insist they pick knives or swords or something to that tune. I do think they could afford to have maybe a little bonus that works with that specialty (maybe fighting finesse with blades, though I could see that getting minmaxy) but it's not terrible, and I feel like a wizened is more likely to come out of arcadia with more experience weilding blades than guns or clubs (the latter seems more fitting for ogres). draconics\u2026 are kind of overpowered, they probably don't need the option to reroll attacks until wyrd evolution.<br /> <br /> I've never really felt like the water-themed kiths have all that much going for them, they're useful enough when you need to go swimming but large bodies of water never really come up in my games, and I have trouble thinking of chronicles where they'd be consistently useful unless it was written with the &quot;well we need to get aquaman in there somehow&quot; mentality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/807-arcadianawakened","name":"ArcadianAwakened","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-02T18:17:13-07:00","id":104495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcadianAwakened</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/97917-balancing-the-kiths-thoughts?p=104468#post104468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least the way I would run things, a specialty in bladed weapons is too broad to have from character creation and I'd insist they pick knives or swords or something to that tune.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even so, it is significantly less potent than pretty much any other combat based Kith. Though Razorhands depends a bit on whether or not you let the specialty they get apply to the weapons they can summon for themselves (as written that Kith is a bit messy).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but it's not terrible, and I feel like a wizened is more likely to come out of arcadia with more experience weilding blades than guns or clubs (the latter seems more fitting for ogres). draconics\u2026 are kind of overpowered, they probably don't need the option to reroll attacks until wyrd evolution. </div> </div> </div>Obviously there are different preferences for how potent a Blessing should be (I think Draconics are fairly close to what I think is a good level for combat focused Kith; though I don't like the thematic nature of their Blessing in the slightest). However a specialty is particularly weak on the grounds that it isn't something you couldn't just buy. An Oracle can buy Common Sense, but that at least gives them access to those mechanics twice as often. A Hunterheart that takes Lethal Mien gets a damage bonus.<br /> <br /> Even if you consider Blades too broad for a Specialty, to benefit from that broadness your character actually needs to use multiple types of blades that would fall under different Specialties otherwise. A character that's a trained swordsman and gets kidnapped to Arcadia to serve in a Fae army... comes back with a slightly broader specialty in Weaponry. Most Kiths at least have some benefit for stacking Blessings with their mundane counterparts.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;Arcadian soldiers = blades&quot; thing, that is a much narrower view of Arcadia than the books present. Arcadia is not CtD's Dreaming that's stuck in perpetual quasi-Medieval fantasy. A Durance could reflect lots of different cultural concepts of being a soldier including ancient cultures that did not use blades as their most symbolic weapons. It could reflect a modern or sci-fi military. However the Soldier Kith does not facilitate any of those.<br /> <br /> In the RPG.net thread I mentioned, I actually suggested radically altering the Kith's Blessing to reflect a more &quot;Wizended&quot; approach to combat. Essentially, something close to True Friend or Playmate with a combat focus. The Wizened Soldier isn't a better fighter, they're a better squad-mate. Which covers any sort of Soldier concept, is something that can easily be done that can synergize with mundane teamwork/group fighting Merits rather than not, and has some meaningful mechanical weight behind it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've never really felt like the water-themed kiths have all that much going for them, they're useful enough when you need to go swimming but large bodies of water never really come up in my games, and I have trouble thinking of chronicles where they'd be consistently useful unless it was written with the &quot;well we need to get aquaman in there somehow&quot; mentality. </div> </div> </div>This is true, but if water is a meaningful part of the game, those Kiths have a very nice bonus.<br /> <br /> That said, something like 80% of humans live near a major body of water (half of the total pop. on coastal alone)... so it isn't that much of a strain to make water relevant to a game. The vast majority of major cities are coastal, on a major river, or on a major lake.<br /> <br /> I think a bigger problem is the nWOD completely lacks decent swimming rules. It's hard to make water-based Kiths mechanically relevant when there's no base-line rules to compare them to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T16:19:55-07:00","id":105162,"title":"","content":"I am considering doing a small tweak to Soldiers as a house rule. Basically, they keep the speciality (I agree it is overly broad for a speciality, but I am fine for it given it is a kith power) and add that Soldiers do not have an penalty for unskilled rolls with Athletics, Brawl, Firearms or Weaponry. I am debating whether to remove Athletics from the list though. Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T16:58:30-07:00","id":105183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/97917-balancing-the-kiths-thoughts?p=105162#post105162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am considering doing a small tweak to Soldiers as a house rule. Basically, they keep the speciality (I agree it is overly broad for a speciality, but I am fine for it given it is a kith power) and add that Soldiers do not have an penalty for unskilled rolls with Athletics, Brawl, Firearms or Weaponry. I am debating whether to remove Athletics from the list though. Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that it's a) the fourth conventional attack-viable Skill and b) fitting with the Wizened thematic of spryness, I'd say Athletics seems to fit fine on the list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T20:53:45-07:00","id":105348,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I like the added &quot;no untrained penalty&quot; bit in general. As noted before, it suffers a serious problem with ceasing to matter once you buy dots in those traits. If they are traits that are central to the concept, it becomes an increasingly meaningless Blessing very quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-03T22:36:49-07:00","id":105383,"title":"","content":"Heavy Arms: I agree, but most players tend to focus on a couple combat traits, not all of them, or put one dot in them to be sort of well rounded. The idea would be they don't need to allocate a point just to alleviate the penalty, they have some innate ability. I've also never seen a PC with dots in all four of those, though I don't doubt they exist, I just don't run combat heavy games. Part of the reason I have four is to hit some bases most PCs won't at least for a bit.<br /> <br /> Thanks both you and Satchel for the feedback","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}